Installation is done like other MikroTik devices: boot an initramfs image over TFTP, and if all works well, flash the final image using sysupgrade. Do NOT upgrade to RouterOS v7, its bootloader is not compatible with OpenWrt; if you upgraded, downgrade to RouterOS v6 before installing OpenWrt.

Warning: To boot OpenWrt on hAP ac², RouteurBoot needs BOOTP and doesn't support DHCP. 
The (Windows) TFTP Software Tiny PXE https://labalec.fr/erwan/?page_id=958 is able to do BOOTP (without DHCP) and is reportet to do well with Mikrotik Devices.

-> [[toh:mikrotik:common|Install OpenWrt on MikroTik devices]]

-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]




===== Debricking =====
Mikrotik Devices can be reverted to stock firmeware / be debricked in an easy way.
Follow the instructions here: https://wiki.mikrotik.com/wiki/Manual:Reset and here https://wiki.mikrotik.com/wiki/Manual:Netinstall

Reset Button, the Mikrotik Netinstall tool and the right firmware file do the job. As Mikrotik uses different plattforms, be sure to get the right package. The hap ac2 is based on Router OS 6, ARM Plattform (32Bit)

Beware: After you flashed the stock firmware, the device has NO configuration. You must connect to the device with the help of Mikrotiks "Winbox" software which uses the MAC Adress (as the device has no IP) .
After Connecting, restore the default configuration and reboot. Then you are ready to start all over again     


