===== Specific configuration =====

==== Network interfaces ====

The basic network interfaces of the hAP ac2 are 5 ethernet interfaces that are connected to the CPU via a switch integrated in the SoC ipq4018, plus two radio circuits, one for 2.4 GHz and one for 5 GHz.
On the encasing they are designated #1 (Internet/PoE in), and #2 - #5 (LAN). Two VLAN IDs have been reserved:
'1' for the LAN ports, 
'2' for the Internet/PoE port

Output from 'swconfig dev switch0 show'
<WRAP BOX 600px>
VLAN 1:
	vid: 1
	ports: 0t 1 2 3 4 
VLAN 2:
	vid: 2
	ports: 0t 5 
</WRAP>
Note that port 0 is the CPU, 5 the Internet/PoE port, and LAN #2 - #5 correspond to ports 4 - 1, so reverse order to what is printed on the casing.  
The default network and wireless configurations that are created provide for disabled wireless, Internet/PoE seeking a dhcp server, and #2 - #5 bridged and assigned 192.168.1.1.
It is possible to define additional VLAN(s) and to assign LAN ports to them, taking them out of the eth0 bridge.
Use other VLAN IDs than 1 and 2 as those are reserved.


